Serve the workbench bundle with an ETag instead of a 1 year cache.

VS Code serves the static files with "Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000"
and the URL of the bundle does not change between builds (it is derived from
the VS Code commit), so after updating the server the browser keeps using the
old bundle. With an ETag the browser revalidates on every load and only
downloads the file again when it really changed. The workbench HTML itself is
sent with "no-store" so the browser never keeps a stale bundle URL.

Index: code-server/lib/vscode/src/vs/server/node/webClientServer.ts
===================================================================
--- code-server.orig/lib/vscode/src/vs/server/node/webClientServer.ts
+++ code-server/lib/vscode/src/vs/server/node/webClientServer.ts
@@ -222,7 +222,14 @@
